Diagnostics recording

Record diagnostics: in the Android drawer (Developer tools), the PC Developer menu, or with Ctrl+F3. It records 15 s to 2 min, or until stopped, and gives a short Markdown report plus the frames as .jsonl, zipped into perf_<game>_<time>.zip. The report is copied to the clipboard.
What the report says:

the device, the GPU and driver, CPU clocks and thermal state, and the settings;
frame-time percentiles;
a CPU/GPU-bound verdict, and how much slower a processor and GPU…

The backfill gate now covers Going Commando (USA v1.01) for boot, title and front-end menu code. Level functions are next.

Interpreter (tools/interpreter/, test-only, never built by the port or launcher):

capture phases, call spreading and call counts;
fcheck now compares from the same kernel and services state, using the capture run's hooks and disc;
a run where every state is skipped no longer counts as SAME;
addresses of the function's own code compare relative to its entry;
instruction…
